| amixdrv_init.s -- the boot chain of the drivers linked into this kernel.
|
| Generated from amixdrv_init.s.in (amix-gate uts/amiga/port/src) by the AMIX
| Installer, or by a relink script, for the drivers chosen: the line
| @INITS@ becomes one `jsr <init>` per driver that has one (KIT.info init=),
| graphics before network.  Assemble with m68k-cbm-sysv4-as, link it after the
| driver objects, then run `patch_io_init.py KERNEL amixdrv_init`.
|
| AMIX's main() walks io_init[] = { parinit, 0 } once at boot; the table has
| no spare slot, so patch_io_init.py retargets its one relocation from parinit
| to amixdrv_init.  parinit (the parallel port, by symbol: whatever parinit is
| in this kernel) runs first, exactly as before, then each driver's probe.
| io_init[] routines take no arguments and their return values are not used;
| each init is C and keeps the registers the C calling convention keeps.
| .text stays a multiple of 4 bytes, so the kernel's .data follows it directly.

	.text
	.globl	amixdrv_init
amixdrv_init:
	jsr	parinit
@INITS@
	rts
	.align	4
